review_text:
Iam actually want to give a thumbs up but there are still many things need to be fixed.

what I like:
- love the art style, its totally cute!
- character customization, we can change clothes and hair styles. there are many options of them;
- we can have babies (max 2) boy or girl, they can grow up and study on school or help our farm or work for other villager and we can collect their wages;
- our wife / husband can do the same thing as above;
- we can go old and died, and we can play as one of our children;
- many 'difficulty' configuration, so you can play the game as you wish. challenging, cozy or relaxing? its your choice and you can change it anytime during the game!

-What I dislike:
- Craftmanship we build is too cheap! its totally not worth to sell;
- no 'nemesis' system. you can insult and make someone as your enemy but their family / legacy wont hate you (if you dont harass them);
- coffee should revover some stamina (or sleepy bar) rather than speed up the movement;
- a bug when you relocate your house somewhere on the farm, when you go out from your house you will spawn at your house origin location (it happened everytime you load the game);
- no sprinkle system (I know sprinkle invented in the end of 1800s and the game is in 1700s, but since the farm is huge, we need a watering system. especially when the farm helpers are in holiday). *yeah I know I can use rain potion. but, still..
- family (farm helpers) cant refill the watering can (you need steel watering can to make it efficient);
- family (farm helpers) cant take care animals;
- cant put object above another object. I want to make outdoor paths and put some fences on it, but it cant.
- event is too few;
- no characters lore (even the ending wont make you sad or feel simpathy because there is no character / relationship building with the NPCs. the NPCs only sell, buy, or give you quests!)
- no sorting system for inventory.

another info:
this game contains DEI.
